WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.480
one of nature's odder creatures is the firefly&nbsp;
a soft-bodied beetle that emits a warm yellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.240
glow from its lower abdomen typically at&nbsp;
twilight in order to attract mates or prey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.880
though relatively rare in europe and north&nbsp;
america the firefly is a common sight in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:27.120
Japan where it is known as the Hotaru, Hotaru&nbsp;
are at their most plentiful in June and July&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.000
and can be seen in groups around rivers and lakes&nbsp;
the glittering light of the Hotaru is deemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.880
to be so enchanting the Japanese hold firefly&nbsp;
festivals or Hotaru matsuri to watch their dance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.160
something even odder has happened to the firefly&nbsp;
in japan, it has become philosophical Zen Buddhist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:52.000
poets and philosophers the two terms are largely&nbsp;
interchangeable in japan have over the centuries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.280
noted the affinity between the firefly and a&nbsp;
central concept in zen the brevity of life zen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.040
does not think of our transients as tragic rather&nbsp;
it is by accommodating ourselves gracefully to our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.160
own evanescence that we can reach enlightenment&nbsp;
and harmony with nature's necessities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:17.280
for zen the firefly is the perfect symbol of&nbsp;
transients positively interpreted its season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.320
is very brief it lights up only in high summer&nbsp;
and its light is intermittent and flickering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.080
fireflies are both fragile and astonishingly&nbsp;
beautiful when seen in large numbers in a pine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.720
forest or a meadow at night they are&nbsp;
a metaphor for our own poignant lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.560
the move of locating important philosophical&nbsp;
themes in the natural world is one that zen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:45.040
makes again and again for example in relation to&nbsp;
bamboo evocative of resilience water a symbol of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:51.120
patient strength capable of wearing down stone&nbsp;
and cherry blossom an emblem of modest rapture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.600
zen repeatedly hangs its ideology onto things that&nbsp;
could seem at first very minor because it wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.520
make use of what is most ordinarily in our sight&nbsp;
to keep us tethered to its grand pathetic truths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:12.640
the great 17th century poet matsuo basho pushes&nbsp;
aside our day-to-day vanity and egoistic ambitions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.160
in the hope that we might become via his focus&nbsp;
on a small short-lived creature appropriately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:28.160
attentive to our own finitude falling from a blade&nbsp;
of grass to fly off a firefly for zen Buddhism the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:34.720
firefly is the ideal carrier on its slender wings&nbsp;
of reminders of the need for dignified resignation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:40.320
in the face of the mightiness and mystery&nbsp;
of the natural order koyabashi issa an 18th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:48.000
century Buddhist priest as well as haiku master&nbsp;
wrote 230 poems on fireflies in one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.920
celebrated of these he captures a moment where&nbsp;
time is momentarily stilled so that its passage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:01.520
can more viscerally be felt the fireflies are&nbsp;
sparkling and even the mouth of a frog hangs wide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:09.120
open it's a tiny moment of satori or enlightenment&nbsp;
the frog is as wonderstruck as the poet at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.680
piercing light of the brave doomed fireflies much&nbsp;
as we should fairly be amazed frightened grateful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.920
and ultimately joyous to have been allocated a few&nbsp;
brief moments in which to behold and try to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:29.120
sense of our own existence in an always largely&nbsp;
unfathomable 13.8 billion year old universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.440
how to survive the modern world is&nbsp;
a guide to coping with the present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:41.600
it explores why some key features of modern&nbsp;
life including capitalism advertising mass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.680
media and the rise of individualism can have&nbsp;
harmful effects on our psychological health

